WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.920
Oh, where should I put this?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.210
The famous wage gap statistic—that for the
same work women earn 77 cents on the dollar—that’s

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.210
bogus.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:17.920
If employers could save 23 percent by hiring
women, they’d fire all the men!

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.550
The gap is just the difference between the
average wages of all working men and women.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.960
It ignores factors that justify different
pay: type of job, hours worked per week.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.200
When these are taken into account, the wage
gap all but disappears.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.679
Now some equal pay activists acknowledge that
factors like college major, hours worked per

00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:39.409
week—that these explain the gap.

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:45.390
But, they insist, women choose different major
and work fewer hours because of social pressure

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.949
and sexist stereotypes.

00:00:46.949 --> 00:00:50.769
Well, it’s 2016, not 1960.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:53.210
American women today are free to choose.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.989
Why not respect their choices?

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:59.589
Now, I’m not suggesting that things are
perfect for women in the work place, but genuine

00:00:59.589 --> 00:01:02.089
reform will come from truth, not myth.

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:09.010
If you want to see progress in the work place,
stop promoting the phony wage gap statistic.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:13.510
What do you think we can do to stop the spread
of misinformation?

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.610
Let me know in the comments, and if you have
ideas for other topics I could cover in 60

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.040
Seconds tell me about that too!

